      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p><strong>Given:</strong></p>\n<p>88% of 370 + 24% of 210 - ? = 118</p>\n<p><strong>Formula used:</strong></p>\n<p>x% of y = <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{x \\times y}{100}\\)</span></p>\n<p><strong>Calculations:</strong></p>\n<p>88% of 370 + 24% of 210 - x = 118</p>\n<p>⇒ <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{88 \\times 370}{100} + \\frac{24 \\times 210}{100} - x = 118\\)</span></p>\n<p>⇒ 325.6 + 50.4 - x = 118</p>\n<p>⇒ 376 - x = 118</p>\n<p>⇒ x = 376 - 118</p>\n<p>⇒ x = 258</p>\n<p><strong>∴ The correct answer is option (2).</strong></p>",
