    {
      "id": "46ad58b97f16-q10",
      "number": 10,
      "question": "A number decreased by \\(\\frac{75}{2}\\%\\) gives 378. What is the number?",
      "questionHtml": "A number decreased by&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{75}{2}\\%\\)</span> gives 378. What is the number?&nbsp;",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "606.4",
          "html": "606.4"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "608.0",
          "html": "608.0"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "603.2",
          "html": "603.2"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "604.8",
          "html": "604.8"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/shortcut-trick-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /> <u style=\"font-size: 21px; font-weight: 700; display: inline !important;\">Shortcut Trick</u></span>\n<p>Fraction value of 37.5% (75/2%) = 3/8.</p>\n<p>This means a decrease of 3 units on the original 8 units.</p>\n<p>Remaining value = 8 − 3 = 5 units.</p>\n<p>Given 5 units → 378</p>\n<p>Original 8 units → (378 ÷ 5) × 8 = 75.6 × 8 = 604.8.</p>\n<p><strong>∴ The correct answer is 604.8.</strong></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/alternate-methord-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Alternate Method</u></span></strong></span></p>\n<p><strong>Given:</strong></p>\n<p>A number decreased by 75/2% gives 378.</p>\n<p><strong>Formula Used:</strong></p>\n<p>Final Value = Original Value × (1 − Decrease%)</p>\n\n<svg width=\"420\" height=\"200\" viewBox=\"0 0 420 200\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"display:block;margin:12px 0;background:#ffffff;border-radius:10px;border:1px solid #cccccc;\">\n  <!-- Original bar -->\n  <rect x=\"40\" y=\"60\" width=\"340\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#ddeeff\" stroke=\"#2255cc\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" />\n  <rect x=\"252.5\" y=\"60\" width=\"127.5\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#fff0cc\" stroke=\"#cc5500\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" />\n  <line x1=\"252.5\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"252.5\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#cc5500\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,3\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" />\n  \n  <!-- Text labels -->\n  <text x=\"146\" y=\"85\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#222222\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Result = 62.5% (5/8)</text>\n  <text x=\"316\" y=\"85\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#cc5500\" text-anchor=\"middle\">− 37.5% (3/8)</text>\n\n  <!-- Brackets below -->\n  <path d=\"M 40 110 L 40 120 L 146 120 L 146 130 M 146 120 L 252.5 120 L 252.5 110\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2255cc\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" />\n  <text x=\"146\" y=\"145\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2255cc\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Value = 378</text>\n  \n  <path d=\"M 40 40 L 40 30 L 210 30 L 210 20 M 210 30 L 380 30 L 380 40\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2255cc\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" />\n  <text x=\"210\" y=\"15\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2255cc\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Original Number = 100% (8/8)</text>\n</svg>\n\n<p><strong>Calculations:</strong></p>\n<p>⇒ Let the required number be x.</p>\n<p>⇒ Decrease % = 75/2% = 37.5%</p>\n<p>⇒ Final value = x − (37.5% of x)</p>\n<p>⇒ x × (100 − 37.5) ÷ 100 = 378</p>\n<p>⇒ x × (62.5 ÷ 100) = 378</p>\n<p>⇒ x × (625 ÷ 1000) = 378</p>\n<p>⇒ x × (5/8) = 378</p>\n<p>⇒ x = 378 × (8/5)</p>\n<p>⇒ x = 75.6 × 8</p>\n<p>⇒ x = 604.8</p>\n<p><strong>∴ The correct answer is 604.8.</strong></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Additional Information</u></span></strong></span></p>\n<p style=\"margin:8px 0 2px 0;font-weight:700;color:#222222;\">Percentage to Fraction Conversion</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px 0;color:#444444;\">Converting standard percentages to fractions significantly reduces calculation steps. For example, 12.5% = 1/8, 37.5% = 3/8, and 62.5% = 5/8.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:8px 0 2px 0;font-weight:700;color:#222222;\">Percentage Decrease Rule</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px 0;color:#444444;\">When a given value decreases by R%, the Final Value can be directly calculated as Original Value × (1 − R/100).</p></p>",
